{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Riders</b> — this is joined with 'the desire of Elohim to dwell in it.'" "And the meaning of רבבות — like 'around Elisha, myriads' [2 Kings 6:17], many myriads." "<b>Thousands</b> — twice in number, like 'a thousand thousands.' And אלף שנאן — the alef is in place of the yod, construct pattern. And some say: that this is an allusion to the number of the Levites in the wilderness, but this is not from the meaning of the psalm." "And the meaning of 'HaShem among them' [is]: the Shekhinah was among them at Sinai in holiness, and the kaf is lacking, like 'and a city of wild asses shall give birth to a man' [Job 11:12]. And so the meaning is: for the holiness of the land of Israel [was] at Mount Sinai."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 68, :notes {3 "The phrase ויחסר כ״ף may alternatively mean that a kaf is to be supplied ('among them' = כי ה׳ בם); the syntax is compressed and the exact parsing uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:14.046115322Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}